I asked -> I think this is getting out of hands. All we need is a very simple use case where we have all of this data and we have been given access to Open AI's LRM plus embedding models. Is that the best use case we can come up with?

LRM Responded -> 
Is this the best use case?
Yes, it is the best one I have found, and you’re right that it has become too complicated. The idea is simple. The layers of gates, briefs, tiers and decision records came from the debate. They are not needed to start.

The simple version
The use case: find the same problem hiding under different names.

What we have: about 140,000 incidents, 25,000 issues and 68,000 actions, all with free text, plus OpenAI’s reasoning model and embedding models.

What we do:

Turn the text of every incident, issue and action into embeddings, so records with similar meaning sit close together.
Find groups of records that are about the same problem but sit in different business units, years or categories.
Use the reasoning model to read each group and write a short summary: what the problem is, where it appears, and what was done about it.
Have two or three experts check the top 20 groups and say whether each is one real problem.
Show the confirmed ones to a senior person and ask whether any of them would change what they do.
That is all.

Why it is worth doing
A normal report can only group by labels and hand-entered links, and those are the inconsistent parts of this data. Embeddings and the reasoning model work on meaning, which is the one thing here that a dashboard cannot do. The result is a list of problems the bank is managing as separate pieces.

How we know if it works
Two questions:

Did it find real problems that the existing labels and categories missed?
Did anyone with authority say “that changes what we do”?
If the answer to either is no, we stop.

Alternatives I considered
Search and Q&A over the data. Simple, but any decent tool does it. Not differentiated.
Concentration reports. A dashboard does this.
Which fixes work. The data cannot support that claim reliably.
Closure review. We lack the closure evidence.
What I’d do next
Skip further design. Take a sample of incidents and issues, run steps 1 to 3 and look at what comes out. A week of that will tell us more than another round of debate. If you can share a sample extract, or tell me who can, I can help set it up.
